<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Havelland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Havelland is a region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, enclosed by the loops of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havel">Havel</a> river. Home of the Slavic Hevelli, whose stronghold was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-an-der-havel">Brandenburg an der Havel</a>, it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> in 1150 and became a core territory of the Margraviate of Brandenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/havelland.jpg" alt="Havelland" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ulamm 17:33, 28 February 2008 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Havelland_FHSW.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
